        "original_id": "6484bbd5-ba01-5cd6-b8c6-fa3e59525df5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Owen Wister, Lucy Maud Montgomery\n- Works: Done in the Open, Anne of Green Gables\n- Topics: western fiction, authorship, publication\n\nFacts:\n- Owen Wister was born on July 14, 1860, and he was an American writer, historian, and the \"father\" of western fiction.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery was born on November 30, 1874, and she was a Canadian author who published as L.M. Montgomery.\n- Done in the Open was a verse collection published in 1903 by the American author Owen Wister.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery became best known for a series of novels that began in 1908 with Anne of Green Gables.\n- Owen Wister died on July 21, 1938.\n- Lucy Maud Montgomery died on April 24, 1942.",
